    "notes": [
      "Scope: evaluation 4 covers the same 12 main-app runs that critic-2 judged (S0 = <app>/20261018-022713, S1 = -s1, S2 = -s2), plus one holdout sample each of docs and landing (20261018-102939). Gates pass in all 14 runs (eval-4.md). Palette consistency is 0.969 / 1.0 / 0.969 and type consistency 0.888 / 0.764 / 0.82. Every holdout finding is '1 of 1'. All of them are minor, so none counts against the prompt.",
      "Main apps: I spot-checked the reshot captures against critic-2 and they are unchanged. The blog S2 home shows FEATURED as a mono label, the plate in the first viewport, and 'New post? One email.' over the dot field (blog/20261018-032252-s2/screenshots/home-desktop-dark.png). The commerce S1 grid has no column repeat, has fact captions, and closes with 'Over $100? Ships free.' (commerce/20261018-032252-s1/screenshots/home-desktop-light.png). The dashboard S0 chart and activity panels end together, the teal OCT column is on a quiet stage, and the table runs flush 272 to 1408 (dashboard/20261018-022713/screenshots/home-desktop-dark.png). Settings S2 billing has 48px group gaps, tier slabs, and an invoice table on the controls column (settings/20261018-032252-s2/screenshots/settings-billing-desktop-light.png). critic-2's recurring items are unchanged and not re-raised: V4 (record-detail caption repeats facts, 2 of 3, spec gap), V5 (in-body plate kind shared with a Related card, 3 of 3, minor), the specKinds diagonal echo, and the bare 'This device' dot on mobile. critic-2 judged none of them blocking. rc.8 and rc.9 already take them up.",
      "Regressions: critic-1 and critic-2 of rc.7 and critic-1 of rc.6 list no open blocker. Their majors (rc.6 R1 settings gap, R2 column repeat) stay fixed 3 of 3. Nothing is worse than published 1.0.0 (0.1.0-rc.3 runs) in two or more samples. 1.0.0 has no holdout runs to compare with.",
      "Update goal (iterations.md, 1.1.0): reached and held. Mobile tables keep two columns, equal rows and an ellipsis rather than a cut, with no ghost '$' (dashboard/*/screenshots/team-mobile-dark.png, projects-mobile-light.png). The about blueprints are about 275px in all three samples. The holdouts carry the same rules: the docs config tables collapse to one stacked column on phones (docs/20261018-102939/screenshots/docs-guides-configuration-mobile-light.png). The landing and docs blueprint rows are measured at 273px (landing agent-report.md; docs/20261018-102939/drawings/home-d1.png).",
      "Holdouts carry the system. Docs: the sidebar has mono group labels and a tinted current item. The home page has a lit stage holding a real task-run table with a scan glyph in the Running row, split openers, a hairline grid of the four groups and a row of three blueprints (stack, marching pair, box). It closes with a two-tone 'Cache once. Run less.' over the dot field. Article pages narrow from the right with a contents rail, a plate--wide lead, numbered mono steps (01-04) and callouts that are hairline boxes. The search popover's empty state uses the dot glyph. Landing: the hero puts the h1 left and two-tone copy right. Its stage is lit from below, holding the product's own week view with dot meters, a scan glyph and a shimmering status (motion-m2, m3). Below come a 'TRUSTED BY' mono strip, split openers, a hairline feature grid and a STEP row of three blueprints with a marching pair (motion-m1). Pricing has tier slabs that go 1-2-3, a segmented Monthly/Yearly toggle and a mono-head comparison table. Customers has a plate grid with eight distinct kinds and fact captions ('NO. 01 · 12 CLINICS'). Sign-up has a dot-meter password strength, an indigo focus ring over red error borders and a '5 fields need attention' banner above the action. Its success state is a joined pair with a two-tone sentence. Compared with pipeline/linear-study/reference/screenshots/p1-desktop-light.png, the landing is the closest of all six apps to the reference.",
      "Measured layout defects, checked. docs / (desktop and mobile) double-rule, figure.stage and div.code-block against div.opener: real, finding 3 (the block's bottom edge fuses with the next opener's rule). docs /changelog double-rule on inline code: real, finding 4. landing uneven-row newsletter field vs Subscribe on /, /pricing, /customers, /signup: real, one finding (1), the same footer on every page. landing / double-rule demo-days vs demo-event (desktop and mobile): real, finding 6. landing / mobile clipped-text '13:00' past figure.stage: false alarm. The window runs off the stage's bottom edge and fades by recipe (Signature 1 'a raised window runs off the bottom edge'), as the reference's hero window does (p1-desktop-light.png). landing / mobile clipped-text 'Proposed · 4 of 4 free' and '10:30 to 11:30' inside div.demo-event: real, finding 5.",
      "Optional fixes for the spec-caused minors, all general. (1) Text field or Button: 'a field and a button in one row share one height: the button takes size.field, or the row aligns both to the taller control'. (2) Typography → Closing statement: 'when the headline is existing copy that must stay, keep it whole in one tone at the closing size, and put the two-tone split in the line under it'. (3) Signature 6 recipe: give a section's last block space above the next opener's rule (for example `.opener{margin-top:var(--space-48)}`, or a bottom padding on the section), so no stage, grid or code block sits on a rule. This is the general form of rc.9's closing-only fix.",
      "Not penalized. Known capture artifacts: the sticky header appears mid-page in full-page captures (docs state-copy-code-mobile-light.png, landing state-faq-open-desktop-dark.png and state-newsletter-error-desktop-light.png, customers filtered mobile). Drawing-crop numbering is off by one (docs and landing drawings/home-d2.png show FIG 0.3). Base-app content is kept as instructed: 'Account Settings', title-case data, and the landing's 'No meetings were harmed' footer. The docs lead plate caption 'NO. 02 · 1 MIN READ' follows the article row. Mobile code blocks scroll horizontally, which is normal for code. The landing agent reports 32px filter chips and header buttons; the spec allows 44px reached through padding, and the screenshots cannot show hit areas.",
      "Scores, descriptive. Reference fidelity 4: the language carries to docs and landing as well as the four apps. Not a 5 because blueprint craft stays below p1-i5, with clean single outlines vs ribbed tiers (docs/20261018-102939/drawings/home-d1.png vs pipeline/linear-study/reference/illustrations/p1-i5.png). Cross-app 4: six apps, one family, with the same openers, mono labels, pills, hairline grids, closings and states. Hierarchy 4: every holdout screen leads with one h1 and a stage or plate. Spacing 4: the main apps hold 48px gaps, while docs has blocks set on the next rule (minor). Component states 4: focus, error, banner, empty search, copied, nav collapse, FAQ open and pricing toggle are all designed. Polish 4: minor one-offs only. Signature 4: every element is present and moving as specified, including the holdout motion (bp-dash marching at 1000ms, scan glyph steps(8), shimmer at 2400ms).",
      "Verdict basis: no blocker, and no major in any sample or holdout. Every finding is minor, so the candidate passes the bar. The update goal holds 3 of 3, and the system carries to the two holdout products."
